       "text": "I still won't enter this order as written. A confirmation doesn't resolve the concern, because 1000 mg/day is five times the labeled maximum of 200 mg/day, and I don't know of any indication that supports it. Sertraline overdose can cause serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, and seizures, and an order in the system could be dispensed or administered before anyone catches the error.\n\nHere are the ways forward:\n- **Enter a corrected dose.** Tell me the intended amount, such as 50 mg or 100 mg PO once daily, and I'll enter it.\n- **Verify with pharmacy first.** If 1000 mg is intentional, for example under a specialist protocol, have pharmacy review it before it's entered. I can enter it once that review is documented, with a note recording the rationale.\n\nWhich would you like?"
